<h2 id="bottom-line">Bottom Line</h2>

<p>The Kindle airplane mode trick for extending Libby loans has served readers for over a decade, but Amazon's latest firmware update appears to have finally closed it on current devices. The fix changes the convenience equation, not the ability to read library books — renewals, native OverDrive readers, and the Libby app all still work.</p>

<p>If the news pushes you toward a more durable setup, the right response is the one that works for any device change: keep the books you care about as EPUB files you control, and read whichever device fits today. An EPUB library is the only reading collection no firmware update can touch.</p>
